# Every layer that states its remainder quantity in the layer's own unit, beside the magnitude its
# own figures give. One row per layer examined, `violates` where the two differ at any of the three
# points.
#
# A stated quantity is the magnitude
#   The rule: a remainder's `quantity` may be `derived`, and where it is stated it equals the
#   magnitude of the remainder in force, the size of the nameplate less the demand. The model
#   already works that figure out from the layer's own demand and nameplate, so a stated quantity
#   restates it, and a restatement that differs from what it restates is a contradiction inside
#   one document.
#
# Compared with the remainder in force
#   The magnitude is read from layers/remainder.sqlc through layers/filed_against_derived.sqlc: on
#   a composed layer that owes an exact remainder it is the one worked out from the parts, and
#   elsewhere the nameplate less the demand from the filed totals. Comparing with the difference of
#   a composed layer's totals would accuse `merge-holding-composition/compute`, whose stated 1414,
#   2857 and 4085.6 are right.
#
# All three points
#   Equality is required at the lowest, the most likely and the highest value, within 1e-9. A
#   quantity is a range, and a stated range that agrees only at its middle still disagrees with the
#   document's own figures.
#
# What it does not examine
#   A quantity filed as a typed blank states nothing to compare. A quantity in a unit other than
#   the layer's is `not comparable` at arithmetic/filed_remainder.sqlc, which the readiness example
#   holds at zero, so it is left to that site rather than compared across units here.
#
# Probe
#   Change `refutation/compute`'s stated quantity from 0.0, 2.8 and 5.0 to 0.0, 2.9 and 5.0. This
#   rule must fire. `examples/witnesses` carries that edit.
-- pm:Remainder/pm:quantity against the magnitude from layers/remainder.sqlc, via
-- layers/filed_against_derived.sqlc.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT l.filing, l.layer,
           abs(l.qty_low  - l.m_low)  > 1e-9
           OR abs(l.qty_mode - l.m_mode) > 1e-9
           OR abs(l.qty_high - l.m_high) > 1e-9                           AS violates,
           format('stated [%s, %s, %s] against a magnitude of [%s, %s, %s]',
                  l.qty_low, l.qty_mode, l.qty_high, l.m_low, l.m_mode, l.m_high) AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(layers/filed_against_derived.sqlc)
    ) l
    WHERE l.qty_low IS NOT NULL
      AND l.qty_unit = l.unit
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'stated_quantity_is_not_the_magnitude'
